"about.eyebrow":"About",
"about.title":"Brand on one side, the indicator on the other. My work happens in between.",
"about.p1":"I came into advertising to write campaigns and found out what moves me is a business problem with an indicator next to it.",
"about.p2":"Today I work in brand strategy, client service and planning at an agency, running three accounts at once, from briefing to approval. Before that I spent time in CRM and social listening across an eight-brand operation, and in project coordination and copywriting at a full-service agency.",
"about.p3":"Along the way I learned to code with AI assistance. I did not become an engineer. I became someone who can take an idea off paper alone and get to a product that works. That is where the three Project ANT platforms came from.",
"about.p4":"The same habit ties it all together: look at the data, understand what it is asking for, and turn that into a decision someone can approve.",
"about.f1k":"Education","about.f1v":"Advertising and Communications, UNIJORGE. Graduating December 2026.",
"about.f2k":"Where I am now","about.f2v":"Brand Strategy, Client Service and Planning at Camila Marketing, Branding e Comunicação.",
"about.f3k":"Languages","about.f3v":"Native Portuguese. Fluent, bilingual English. Intermediate Spanish.",
"about.f4k":"How I work","about.f4v":"Data, business case, decision, execution, and the number at the end.",

"areas.eyebrow":"What I do",
"areas.title":"Six fronts, run together.",
"areas.lede":"They hold each other up. Strategy needs data to get approved, data needs a product to become routine, and the product needs someone who understands the brand or it turns into a pretty, useless dashboard.",
"a1t":"Brand Strategy and Marketing",
"a1d":"Positioning, archetypes, tone of voice and 360º planning. I build the rationale before the asset and defend it with a business argument.",
"a1c":"Brand Strategy|Positioning|Brand Archetypes|Brand Equity|Brand Voice|360º Planning|Share of Voice|Top of Mind|Experience Marketing|Copywriting|Trendjacking|Cultural Fluency",
"a2t":"Business Development and Growth",
"a2d":"Performance, funnel and conversion reading applied to decisions on content, format and distribution. An opportunity with no budget is growth too.",
"a2c":"Business Development|Business Case|Go-to-Market|Funnel and Conversion|Performance|Consumer Centricity|Community Engagement|Client Service|Market Research|Briefing",
"a3t":"Data, Analytics and Performance",
"a3d":"Reading indicators, designing KPIs and reporting to whoever decides. I prefer one number that holds up a choice over ten that decorate a slide.",
"a3c":"Data Analysis|Business Intelligence|KPI Design|Power BI|Google Analytics|Meta Business Suite|SQL|Executive Reporting|Competitive Analysis",
"a4t":"Social Listening and Consumer Insights",
"a4d":"Interaction tagging, sentiment analysis and detraction reading at scale. People complaining are usually telling the brand exactly what to do next.",
"a4c":"Social Listening|Sentiment Analysis|Brand Detraction|Buzzmonitor|Crisis Management|Consumer Behaviour|Community Management|Consumer Insights",
"a5t":"Projects, Products and Leadership",
"a5d":"Flow, deadlines, dependencies and quality across teams that don't speak the same language. I've led a 30-person team and run accounts from diagnosis to delivery.",
